            <ArticleTitle>Drooping of the big toe: another diagnostic marker for L-5 radiculopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Drooping of the big toe is found in a host of neurologic diseases. If found in isolation in a patient who has low back pain, with or without clear sensory deficit, this finding can be a useful, objective aid in localizing the lesion to the L-5 nerve root.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
